# task-7c088f59 current recurrence — 2026-09-29 (8 demos, unresolved)

Test grid was 29x8, bg5. Color-9 boundary bars: top row r0 c6-7; bottom row r28 c0-1. Color-2 singleton seeds at (r3,c0) and (r12,c1). The instance ended after 8 demos and 8 incorrect submissions; no output is validated.

## Exact demos and observed changes (0-indexed)
1. 12x8 bg2: left vertical 1 bar r0-4,c0; right vertical 1 bar r6-10,c7; isolated 0s at (7,5),(9,5). Output adds 0 across r1 and r3, c1-7; for each isolated 0, changes its cell to 4 and adds 4 immediately to its left at c5. Bars remain.
2. 6x19 bg8: boundary-color 2 bars r0,c14-18 and r5,c5-9. Color9 seeds (1,6),(2,5),(2,8-9). Output maps those seeds to 4 and extends color9 downward: broad local 2x2-ish blocks/stripes at c5-6 and c8-9, plus copies/fills of right bar shape down rows1-5 at c14-18. This is not simply painting all lines from each seed.
3. 21x16 bg3: color6 bars right c15,r11-13 and left c0,r18-20. Color9 seeds (12,6),(13,2). Output expands color9 broadly rightward from each seed across the right-side field (including r12 c7-14 and r13 c3-14), changing each seed's immediate left cell (c5 and c1) to4; extends bottom bar color6 across much of rows19-20 c1-15. Exact grouping is selective.
4. 22x9 bg0: 6 bars top r0 c4-6 and bottom r21 c0-2; color7 seeds (3,6),(16,5),(18,4). Output fills vertical color7 strips at c0-2 rows0-20 (preserving bars), and c4-5 rows1-15; seeds become4. Selective columns, not all seed rays.
5. 7x6 bg0: 7 bars right c5,r2-3 and left c0,r5-6; color2 seeds (2,1),(3,2). Output fills color2 broad horizontal/rectangular regions: r2 c2-4, r3 c3-4, plus r5-6 c1-5. Each seed changed to4. Bars persist.
6. 19x13 bg8: 1 bars top r0 c4-7 and bottom r18 c0-3; color9 seeds (5,5),(6,6),(14,7),(17,4). Output paints left region c0-3 rows0-17 and c4-6 rows1-17 in color9; seeds become4. Not all seed-containing columns painted uniformly; note r6 c5-6 remain bg8 while r7-13 c5-6 filled.
7. 10x6 bg2: top row has bg0 pair c0-1 and color2 c2-5; bottom row r9 has bg0 pair c3-4. Singleton 1 at (1,3). Output fills color1 down c0 rows1-8 and c3 rows2-8, changes singleton (1,3) to4; bar colors/pairs preserved.
8. 7x13 bg2, bars color8 top-left r0 c0-4 and bottom r6 c6-10; sparse color3 at (1,7),(3,8). Output fills color3 rectangle c1-2 rows1-6; extends color3 vertically c7 rows2-5 and c8 rows4-5. Both seed cells become4. Bars preserved.

## Important inference / caveat
Across demos, multiple different colors/positions of boundary bars and seeds occur. Seed(s) often change to 4, but several demos have seeds retained or different seed subsets, and painted areas vary among horizontal/vertical stripes, rectangles, and projections. No selector or general rule was identified. Do not reuse guessed test outputs or assume the two color-2 seeds both convert to4, nor use no-op: the test's 8 submissions (all incorrect) included these exact attempts/hypotheses:
1) filled 2x2 patches around seeds and changed them to4;
2) broad vertical c4 stripe and horizontal c5-7 region, seeds->4;
3) unchanged grid;
4) seeds->4 and rightward row projections;
5) downward columns from seeds;
6) broad diagonal/down-right rectangle projections;
7) vertical/rightward large fill from seeds;
8) seeds->4 only.
All failed. Prior attempts do not isolate selector; rule remains unresolved. Future recurrence: record complete deltas and negative evidence, formulate selector before submission, don't cycle these guesses. Current instance consumed all 8 demos and 8 wrong submissions; task finished unsolved.
